<article class="env-lemma" id="02OY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02OY">Lemma <span data-tag="02OY">31.24.8</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of locally ringed spaces. Assume that pullbacks of meromorphic functions are defined for $f$ (see Definition <a href="/tag/02OT" data-tag="02OT">31.24.4</a>). </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-modules. There is a canonical pullback map $f^* : \Gamma (Y, \mathcal{K}_ Y(\mathcal{F})) \to \Gamma (X, \mathcal{K}_ X(f^*\mathcal{F}))$ for meromorphic sections of $\mathcal{F}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-module. A regular meromorphic section $s$ of $\mathcal{L}$ pulls back to a regular meromorphic section $f^*s$ of $f^*\mathcal{L}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>